expanded_source_wording_tex:
\label{def:primitive-roles}
The six primitive closure roles are
\begin{itemize}[topsep=2pt,itemsep=1pt]
  \item \ensuremath{\mathrm{P1}} --- update-vs-quotient compatibility / descent
    obstruction~\citep{GrothendieckSGA1,JanelidzeTholen1994};
  \item \ensuremath{\mathrm{P2}} --- macro-specification
    representability~\citep{MacLane1998};
  \item \ensuremath{\mathrm{P3}} --- enriched route/coherence
    mismatch~\citep{BaaderNipkow1998,Nakahara2003}; \ensuremath{\mathrm{P3}} is not a
    directionality certificate;
  \item \ensuremath{\mathrm{P4}} --- stage/order/transition/refinement
    structure~\citep{Milner1989,BackVonWright1998};
  \item \ensuremath{\mathrm{P5}} --- quotient packaging /
    quotienting~\citep{KemenySnell1960};
  \item \ensuremath{\mathrm{P6}} --- audit/bookkeeping/provenance/replay/checkability~\citep{GreenKarvounarakisTannen2007,Merkle1987}.
\end{itemize}

